{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_fvqxofazu32nkhk3pgrbqeprajir4vh5r6mtwvliqihvrfhkqrkq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — all four phases done and independently checked on disk.\n\n## What the library is\n\n`c_src` compiles one file (`src/lib.c`) into a shared object exporting exactly **two** symbols: `tflac_size_memory(u32) -> u32` (pure wrapping arithmetic) and `flac_validate(tflac*) -> int` (11 sequential range checks plus in-place mutation of `channel_mode`, `max_rice_value`, `partition_order`, `cur_blocksize`).\n\n## Phase A artifacts (crate root)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — `nm -D` for both `.so`s. C exports `flac_validate`, `tflac_size_memory`; Rust exports both with identical names → **symbol diff empty, 0 stubs**. Also records the C struct layout verified with an `offsetof` program (size 28, align 4, padding at 21..23) against the Rust `#[repr(C)]`.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 20 rows: the 11 `return -1` branches (matching `grep -c 'return -1'` = 11), 2 ordering/precedence rows, and 7 generic-FFI rows (NULL, all 256 `channel_mode` \"enum\" values, one-past-every-boundary, all-zero/all-ones images, padding preservation, `tflac_size_memory` extremes, double-call).\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 30 rows: overflow regimes of `tflac_size_memory`; the full channel-mode decision matrix (mode × channels × bitdepth, including modes 4..255); `max_rice_value` auto-derivation at the `<=16` boundary; the partition-order loop keyed on `blocksize`'s 2-adic valuation; boundary values, garbage output fields/padding, valid + raw fuzz, repeated calls, and the composed validate→size pipeline.\n\n## Phases B/C/D — tests in `translation/tests/`\n\nBoth libraries are loaded with `libloading` and called only through their exported symbols; every assertion compares the return value **and all 28 struct bytes** (padding included). 56 tests pass (30 config rows, 23 error tests, 3 symbol-parity tests), plus 4 `#[ignore]`d exhaustive sweeps that verify **all 2^32** `tflac_size_memory` inputs and ~42 M `flac_validate` cases.\n\n`run_all.sh` automates the whole matrix: `{default, --no-default-features}` × `{rust debug, rust release}` × `{CMake C build, extra -O2 C build}` + `EXHAUSTIVE=1`. Final run: **44/44 test-result lines ok, 0 failures, symbol diff empty** (`Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`, so those two combos are the complete set).\n\n## One real divergence found and fixed (Rust only)\n\n`flac_validate(NULL)`: the C faults with `SIGSEGV`, but the Rust `.so` aborted with `SIGABRT` — the translation started with `let t = &mut *t;`, and reference creation makes rustc emit a debug-assertion null check (\"null pointer dereference occurred\"). Caught by a fork-based differential test (`err_14`). Fixed by accessing fields only through the raw pointer (`ptr::read`/`ptr::write` on `addr_of!((*t).field)`), so an invalid `t` now faults identically in **both debug and release**. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified (only the required `build/` output)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":405,"cache_read_input_tokens":110371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":405,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eea6ab85-ffb8-4b22-9624-37c74530e0e8","uuid":"8d30dea7-487b-44e5-8a7e-0f60b3c1f1ad","timestamp":"2026-08-26T21:25:45.539Z"}
